To extract the exact definition of "artificial intelligence" from the given JSON data, you can use the following Java code:
```
import org.json.*;
public class AIAssistant {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 String jsonString = "{"Title":"Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach","Authors":[{"Name":"Stuart Russell","Affiliation":"University of California, Berkeley"},{"Name":"Peter Norvig","Affiliation":"Google Inc."}],"Abstract":"This textbook provides a comprehensive overview of the field of artificial intelligence, including its history, core concepts, and current research areas. It covers topics such as machine learning, natural language processing, and robotics, among others. The book also includes case studies and exercises to help readers deepen their understanding of the subject.","Keywords":["Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning","Natural Language Processing","Robotics"]}";
 JSONObject obj = new JSONObject(jsonString);
 String abstractText = obj.getString("Abstract");
 String[] sentences = abstractText.split(".");
 String definition = "";
 for(String sentence : sentences) {
 if(sentence.contains("artificial intelligence")) {
 definition = sentence;
 break;
 }
 }
 System.out.println("Definition of Artificial Intelligence: " + definition);
 }
}
```
This code first creates a JSONObject from the given JSON string. Then it extracts the abstract text from the object and splits it into individual sentences. It then searches for the sentence that contains the phrase "artificial intelligence" and extracts it as the definition.
